{
  "requirement": "The `habeas` skill's reference on distributed requirements MUST give the guidance of {cite}`requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.when`, {cite}`requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.queries`, {cite}`requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.site_text`, and {cite}`requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.reviews` as a list of things to do and a list of things not to do.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** `requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.lists` requires the `habeas` skill's distributed-requirements reference to give the guidance of `when`, `queries`, `site_text` and `reviews` as a list of things to do and a list of things not to do. That gives two testable parts. The first is structure: a do-list and a don't-list in that reference. The second is that the four cited requirements' guidance appears in those lists. The cited requirements are context. Their detailed wording is checked by their own tests.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_give_distributed_guidance_as_do_and_dont_lists]` carries `{test}` for the subject. It reads `distributed_reference()`, which is `habeas/references/distributed-requirements.md`, so it targets the right file.\n- **Structure.**\n  - It splits out the `## Do` and `## Don't` sections and requires at least two `- ` bullet items in each.\n  - Every Do item must start with `- ` and must not start with `- Don't `.\n  - Every Don't item must start with `- Don't `.\n  - A missing list, a non-list section, or a misplaced item would fail.\n- **Content mapping.** Through `assert_text` on `section(...)` for each heading, it asserts phrases that I confirmed in the reference text:\n  - `when`: Do has \"Make a requirement distributed only when\" and \"Separate obligations each site upholds\". That second item covers the `{impl}` instruction.\n  - `queries`: Do has \"Write a violation query\", \"Give every query `match` and `no_match` snippets\", and the check that site queries \"select every place the obligation applies and no others\".\n  - `site_text`: Do has \"Describe sites exactly as the site queries select them\". Don't has \"Don't describe sites more broadly\" and \"Don't state a per-site obligation\".\n  - `reviews`: Do has \"Let `habeas author --all` author the site reviews.\". Don't has \"Don't reference the distributed requirement from a site\" and \"Don't re-run a false site review for a different result\".\n\n**Assessment.** A reference that dropped a list, left guidance outside the lists, or put a Don't item under Do would fail an assertion. Each of the four cited requirements has at least one asserted item in the lists. The finer wording of each is covered by the sibling requirements' tests, so it does not need repeating here. I found no unaddressed obligation, no wrong expectation and no marking gap. There are no acknowledgments.",
  "references": "09b4c02f269ff2667ff5936f00c7be02a72aa69ffdf977e6ec2025e2db17ad6c",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.lists",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.lists"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} distributed_guidance.lists",
        "The `habeas` skill's reference on distributed requirements MUST give the guidance of {cite}`requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.when`, {cite}`requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.queries`, {cite}`requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.site_text`, and {cite}`requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.reviews` as a list of things to do and a list of things not to do.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.when",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.when"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} distributed_guidance.when",
        "The bundled skills MUST direct agents to make a requirement distributed only when its obligation applies on its own at each of many sites, such as a convention every validation function follows; to use `{impl}` instead when particular code carries out the requirement as a whole; and to mark with `{impl}` the code that carries out any obligation of a distributed requirement that its sites do not uphold.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.queries",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.queries"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} distributed_guidance.queries",
        "The bundled skills MUST direct agents to write site queries that select every place the obligation applies and no others, violation queries for every kind of construct that could break it, and, for every query, `match` and `no_match` snippets that test its conditions.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.site_text",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.site_text"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} distributed_guidance.site_text",
        "The bundled skills MUST direct agents to describe sites exactly as the site queries select them, to state as an obligation any convention the queries rely on, such as how a list is named, and to state only per-site obligations that a reviewer can check from the site and the helpers it calls.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.reviews",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.reviews"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} distributed_guidance.reviews",
        "The bundled skills MUST tell agents that sites need no reference to the requirement, that `habeas author --all` authors site reviews under {cite}`requirements.references.site_review`, and that a false site review is addressed by fixing the site, or by tightening the queries or the requirement text when the site should not be covered or the text admits more than one reading, under {cite}`requirements.cli.flip_guidance`, not by re-running the review.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
